<title>USA: Envirodyne amends by-laws on nominations.</title>
<headline>Envirodyne amends by-laws on nominations.</headline>
<dateline>OAK BROOK, Ill. 1997-03-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Envirodyne Industries Inc said its board amended the company's by-laws, establishing a time frame of 90 to 120 days prior to the annual meeting for stockholders to nominate directors.</p>
<p>The by-laws previously did not address the issue.</p>
<p>For the May 16, 1997 annual meeting, however, the amended by-laws provide that the stockholder's notice to the secretary of any nomination or other business must be received by the company on or before March 28.</p>
<p>((Reuters Chicago Newsdesk (312) 408-8787))</p>
